# No Mock Data in Application Code

Never use fake application data such as hardcoded users, appointments, phone numbers, profiles, call records, KB results, mock API responses, artificial delays, random success responses, or hardcoded tool-call results.

Production code must use real environment config, database records, LiveKit sessions, OpenAI connections, Twilio/SIP integrations, external APIs, and business services.

Mocks, stubs, fixtures, and fake providers are allowed only inside test files.

Do not silently fall back to mock data when an integration fails. Return a controlled error, log the failure, and follow the configured fallback or human-handoff policy.

Do not create demo-only implementations, placeholders, fake integrations, mock services, or mock data unless explicitly requested for automated tests.
